# Alt 5 — Org out of the sidebar entirely

**Move org switching to the top app bar; the sidebar bottom becomes user-only.** The workspace becomes a pill next to the page title (where breadcrumbs/scope usually live). The sidebar footer is then unambiguously one thing: the user.

### Top content header (new home for the org)

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Dashboard          [ ▢ Acme Inc ⌄ ]      🔔  ?  │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Org pill clicked (dropdown down, in context)

```
   [ ▢ Acme Inc ⌃ ]
   ╭─────────────────────────╮
   │  ✓ Acme Inc             │
   │    Globex Corp          │
   │  + New organization     │
   ╰─────────────────────────╯
```

### Sidebar bottom (user only — unchanged shape, half the rows)

```
│  …nav…                        │
├───────────────────────────────┤
│ (GD) Greg Daniels         ↗  │
│      greg@acme.com            │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

### Collapsed sidebar
Footer is a single user avatar; org no longer needs sidebar space at all.

```
│(GD)│
```

**Pros:** cleanest separation — sidebar = me, top bar = where I am; org switch stays one click and sits next to the data it scopes; bottom is genuinely a single item.
**Cons:** requires a top app bar to exist (new surface if there isn't one today); org becomes less "global-feeling," more page-scoped; two surfaces to maintain.
